# GENERAL E.1.f main
# E.1.f - Order is sent to exchange, held waiting for activation and then activated
# Variant note: primary path from the non-italic rows
# Source: https://www.fixtrading.org/online-specification/order-state-changes/

# 1: Entry of a stop (OrdType = 3), stop limit (OrdType = 4), At the Close (TimeInForce = 7), etc, order. E.g. an order that is held off the book waiting for activation subject to specified conditions.
8=FIX.4.49=21635=D49=BUY156=SELL134=152=20240101-09:30:00.00011=CL-e_1_f_order_is_sent_to_exchange_held_waiting_for_activation_and_then_activated-X21=155=IBM54=160=20240101-09:30:01.00038=1000040=399=49.5015=USD59=010=119

# 2: Trader / exchange acknowledge receipt of order but does not enter it into the book at activation conditions are not met (WorkingIndicator = N). Note that if the conditions are met on entry, this WorkingIndicator is not sent.
8=FIX.4.49=39835=849=SELL156=BUY134=152=20240101-09:30:00.00037=ORD-e_1_f_order_is_sent_to_exchange_held_waiting_for_activation_and_then_activated11=CL-e_1_f_order_is_sent_to_exchange_held_waiting_for_activation_and_then_activated-X17=EX-e_1_f_order_is_sent_to_exchange_held_waiting_for_activation_and_then_activated-AUTO001150=039=0636=N55=IBM54=138=1000040=399=49.5032=0151=1000014=06=50.0010=199

# 3: Activation conditions are reached. Trader / exchange acknowledge that order is put on book (WorkingIndicator = Y). Note that this message can be implicit in situations where there is an immediate fill or partial fill (as any state other than New / Pending New means the order has been added to the book and is working).
